│ nulliparous). The mean pain score on a 0-100 mm visual analog scale during insertion in the vaginal delivery group   │
│ was 34.7 (SD 31.6) compared with 51.2 (SD 29.2) in the group without previous vaginal delivery (p = 0.009). In       │
│ multivariable analysis controlling for age, breast-feeding, expected pain, baseline anxiety, insertion timing (6-12  │
│ weeks postpartum, 2-4 weeks post-abortion or interval), and insertion difficulty, history of vaginal delivery was    │
